   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Neon Flicker Text\n\nLights a word tube by tube like a neon sign, with a mains hum that never quite settles and a dying flicker on the way out.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A word or short phrase should read as a neon sign: nightlife, retro, arcade, a late-night offer.\n- You want per-letter ignition with a living hum while it holds.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The sign must be one connected glass tube drawn along a path: use neon-sign.\n- The tone is calm or corporate.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Open late.\"\n- font_size (number, 24-260): Font size, default 96\n- color (color): Color, default \"#fdf2f8\"\n- font_weight (number, 100-900): Font weight, default 700\n- font (enum): Font, default \"geist\"\n- mode (enum): Split by, default \"chars\"\n- order (enum): Order, default \"start\"\n- stagger_frames (number, 0-20): Stagger, default 4\n- duration_frames (number, 1-90): Unit duration, default 24\n- delay_frames (number, 0-120): Delay, default 6\n- exit (boolean): Exit, default true\n- glow_color (color): Glow color, default \"#f472b6\"\n- glow_size (number, 0-120): Glow size, default 26\n- off_level (number, 0-0.6): Off level, default 0.14\n- hum (number, 0-0.6): Hum, default 0.12\n- buzz (number, 0-0.5): Buzz, default 0.06\n- flicker_on_exit (boolean): Flicker out, default true\n\nSource: https://github.com/riaz37/remotion-ui. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
